            <ArticleTitle>Imidazopyridines: a novel class of hNav1.7 channel blockers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1696-701</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2008.01.047</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of imidazopyridines were evaluated as potential sodium channel blockers for the treatment of neuropathic pain. Several members were identified with good hNa(v)1.7 potency and excellent rat pharmacokinetic profiles. Compound 4 had good efficacy (52% and 41% reversal of allodynia at 2 and 4h post-dose, respectively) in the Chung rat spinal nerve ligation (SNL) model of neuropathic pain when dosed orally at 10mg/kg.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
